# No Lodash

Do NOT import or use lodash in this codebase. All lodash functions have vanilla JS replacements.

## When you encounter or are about to write a lodash import

1. STOP — do not add any `import ... from "lodash/..."` or `require("lodash...")`
2. Use **@humansignal/core** for all replacements — all lodash-replacement helpers live there.
3. Import from core: `import { debounce, throttle, clamp, camelCase, snakeCase, kebabCase, capitalize, uniqBy, get, isMatch } from "@humansignal/core"`
4. For cloneDeep use native `structuredClone(obj)`.

## Quick reference (all from @humansignal/core except cloneDeep)

- uniqBy, throttle, debounce, clamp, get, isMatch: @humansignal/core
- camelCase, snakeCase, kebabCase, capitalize: @humansignal/core
- cloneDeep(obj): structuredClone(obj) (native)
